G3120.def:
μαλακός, -ή, -όν 
[in LXX: Proverbes 25:15 (רַךְ) Proverbes 26:22 (לָהַם)* ;] 
soft; 
__1. prop., to the touch (opposite to σκληρός): of clothing, pl., Matthieu 11:8, Luc 7:25. 
__2. Of persons and their mode of living; 
__(a) mild, gentle; 
__(b) soft, effeminate: 1 Corinthiens 6:9 (prob. in obscene sense, cf. Deiss., LAE, 150, 4; MM, xvi; Zorell, see word).†

G3128G.def:
Μανασσῆς, -ῆ, ὁ (Heb. מְנַשֶּׁה), 
Manasseh; 
__1. (a) the first-born son of Joseph; 
__(b) the tribe which bore his name: Apocalypse 7:6. 
__2. King of Judah: Matthieu 1:10.†

G3128H.def:
Μανασσῆς, -ῆ, ὁ (Heb. מְנַשֶּׁה), 
Manasseh; 
__1. (a) the first-born son of Joseph; 
__(b) the tribe which bore his name: Apocalypse 7:6. 
__2. King of Judah: Matthieu 1:10.†

G3173.def:
μέγας, μεγάλη, μέγα, 
[in LXX chiefly for גָּדוֹל, also for מַרְבֶּה ,רַב (incl. μείζων), רֹב (μέγιστος) ;] 
great; 
__1. of external form, bodily size, measure, extent: λίθος, Matthieu 2:60; δράκων, Apocalypse 12:3; ἰχθῦς, Jean 21:11; πόλις, Apocalypse 11:8; μάχαιρα, Apocalypse 6:4, al. 
__2. Of intensity and degree: δύναμις, Actes 4:33; φόβος, Marc 4:41; ἀγάπη, Jean 15:13; ἄνεμος, 'ib. 6:18; κραυγή, Actes 23:9; φῶς, Matthieu 4:16; πυρετός, Luc 4:38; θλίψις, Matthieu 24:21. 
__3. Of rank; 
__(a) of persons: θεός (MM, xvi), Tite 2:13; Ἄρτεμις, Actes 19:27; compar. (see infr.), Matthieu 18:1 (cf. Dalman, Words, 113f.); neut. for masc. (Bl., §32, 1), Matthieu 12:6; 
__(b) of things: ἁμαρτία, Jean 19:11; μυστήριον, Éphésiens 5:32; = μεγίστη (see infr., and cf. Field, Notes, 16f.), Matthieu 22:36; compar. for superl. (M, Pr., 78), 1 Corinthiens 13:13. 
__4. 
__(a) Compar., μείζων: Matthieu 11:11 23:17, al.; neut. pl., μείζονα, contr. μείζω, Jean 1:51; double compar., μειζότερος (M, Pr., 236; Bl., §11, 4), III Jo 4; 
__(b) superl, μέγιστος (Deiss., BS, 365), 2 Pierre 1:4.

G3195.def:
μέλλω, 
[in LXX: Job 3:8 (עָתִיד) 19:25 (אַחֲרוֹן); elsewhere for fut., and frequently in Wi, II, 4Mac ;] 
to be about to be or do; 
__1. with inf. (Bl., §62, 4; 68, 2; M, Pr., 114); 
__(a) of intending or being about to do of one's own free will: with inf. praes., Matthieu 2:13, Luc 10:1, Actes 3:3 5:35, Hébreux 8:5, 2 Pierre 1:12 (Field, Notes, 240), al.; with inf. aor. (Bl., §58, 3), Actes 12:6, Apocalypse 3:16; 
__(b) of compulsion, necessity or certainty: with inf. praes., Matthieu 16:27, Luc 9:31, Jean 6:71, Romains 4:24, al.; with inf. aor., Romains 8:18, Galates 3:23, Apocalypse 3:2 12:4. 
__2. Ptcp., ὁ μέλλων: absol., Romains 8:38, 1 Corinthiens 3:22; τὰ μ., Colossiens 2:17; εἰς τὸ μ. (Field, Notes, 65); with subst., Matthieu 3:7 12:32 (ὁ αἰὼν ὁ μ.; LXX for עַד), Actes 24:25, 1 Timothée 4:8, Hébreux 2:5, al.
